 :findings
 [{:id :closed-record-validation-and-input-totality :locations ["oikos-owner-authority.el:20-24,31-43" "oikos-owner-authority-test.el:37-42"]
   :finding "Only invocation/resource closed shapes are partly validated; the permit and V3 also require identity, approval, grant, revoke request/result and release shapes and relationships. Transcript reads fields via assq before confirming inv and nested resource are well-formed lists, so malformed inputs can signal instead of returning nil. The existing three negative tests do not cover those boundaries."
   :minimal-fix "Add bounded, total, non-mutating closed validators for each selected synthetic shape and its operation/scope/epoch/digest relationships; guard structure before lookup and turn malformed/cyclic/improper/wrong-type inputs into a fixed denial. Keep proposed proof records synthetic data, never claim authenticity. Test unknown/duplicate/missing keys, wrong types and noncanonical data with exact denial and positive controls."}
  {:id :binding-and-snapshot :locations ["oikos-owner-authority.el:31-79" "oikos-owner-authority-test.el:20-42"]
   :finding "The model emits a transcript but never retains an immutable copy or checks digest AND exact transcript again at issue/final use; attempt receives no invocation, approval, identity, resource or release decision at all. Consequently it cannot reject actor/credential/channel/resource/destination/bytes substitution or demonstrate approved request binding. Contract digest shape is checked, not compared to an approved pin. The single golden exercises replace encoding only."
   :minimal-fix "Model pure issuance and final comparison with separately copied closed inputs, explicit expected contract pin, transcript-byte equality and digest, and synthetic provenance tags that grant no real authority. Add read and replace vectors plus independent-byte/digest comparisons, mutable-copy and per-field swap negatives, including same actor/different credential and mismatched destination. UTF-8 range boundaries require explicit synthetic resource bytes; reject unavailable or invalid boundaries rather than infer them from byte length."}
  {:id :read-write-single-use-and-order :locations ["oikos-owner-authority.el:81-107" "oikos-owner-authority-test.el:44-54"]
   :finding "Attempt has no operation or grant identity, only caller-supplied state, and returns the same zero-count marker for read and write. Its consumed test manually supplies consumed, not the returned state of a first read/write; no model of first simulated release, output bytes, competing consumers, revoke ordering, restart or storage outcomes exists. Therefore the permit's read-specific single use and ordering are not exercised despite a generic terminal-state branch."
   :minimal-fix "Introduce a small pure event/state transition model, not an auth engine or ledger: explicitly represent read versus replace, grant identity, consume and simulated first release/mutation; feed returned state into a second attempt. Table-test exact positive read/write and replay, revoke before/concurrent/after, invalidated revoke non-ACK, competing attempts, restart and storage failure with effect/release counts and owner order. No fake persistence claim."}
  {:id :clock-validity-and-history :locations ["oikos-owner-authority.el:87-105" "oikos-owner-authority-test.el:44-54"]
   :finding "Clock validates an independently supplied uncertainty <=1000 and interval width <=2000, but never relates uncertainty to that interval: (10 2010 5 0 t) is accepted as a zero-uncertainty reading if deadlines permit. No previous clock reading is accepted, so monotonic regression, UTC rollback and discontinuity cannot be detected; only one generic UTC and monotonic deadline are checked instead of all applicable grant/approval/credential/policy deadlines."
   :minimal-fix "Specify and enforce a consistent synthetic interval/uncertainty representation with prior trusted reading and conservative discontinuity checks, plus all applicable deadlines for read and write. Add zero-uncertainty/inconsistent interval, oversized uncertainty, regression, rollback, equality, missing clock, restart and separate credential/policy expiry negatives. A fake time model is not a trusted clock adapter."}
  {:id :consume-and-final-gap :locations ["oikos-owner-authority.el:87-107" "oikos-owner-authority-test.el:44-52"]
   :finding "The gap argument models delay after one clock sample, but there is no separate post-consume storage interval or fresh final observation; a check that is expired at entry returns invalidated, so the required case fresh before consume and expired during consumption cannot be expressed while retaining consumed. The existing gap test is not that oracle and has no read-specific assertion."
   :minimal-fix "Split synthetic pre-consume, consume outcome, fresh final clock and final-gap observations; after simulated successful consumption, expiry or uncertainty at the later check denies with consumed terminal state. Test both operation variants and separate post-consume expiry and post-final-check expiry, with unexpired positives and zero simulated effects/release on denial. This is not a real scheduler or atomic-fence proof."}]
